<title>FINLAND: Nokia 1996 profit falls 21 percent.</title>
<headline>Nokia 1996 profit falls 21 percent.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31-</p>
<p>					   (million markka unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit before tax, minority interest     3,898 vs 4,933</p>
<p> Earnings per share (markka)		  10.73 vs 14.36</p>
<p> Net sales					 39,321 vs 36,810</p>
<p> Operating profit				 4,266 vs 5,012</p>
<p> Dividend (markka)				 3.50 vs 3.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' median forecast for Finnish telecoms group Nokia Oy had been for a 3,851 million markka profit before tax and minorities (mean 3.88 billion, range 3.30-4.92 billion).  </p>
<p> Cost of goods sold			    28,029 vs 25,518</p>
<p> Research and development expenses	  3,514 vs 2,531</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses		     3,512 vs 3,749 charge</p>
<p> Share of results of associated firms   gain 37 vs 85 gain</p>
<p> Financial items			   charge 405 vs 164 charge</p>
<p> Tax						    856 vs 769</p>
<p> Minority interests			    gain 2 vs 77 charge</p>
<p> Profit from continuing operations	  3,044 vs 4,087</p>
<p> Discontinued operations		   gain 219 vs 2,340 charge</p>
<p>Profit from ordinary activities before</p>
<p>cumulative effect of change in</p>
<p>  accounting policies			   3,263 vs 1,747</p>
<p>Cumulative prior year effect (after tax)</p>
<p>  of change in accounting policies	    nil vs 485 gain</p>
<p> Net profit					 3,263 vs 2,232</p>
<p>NOTE - Full company name is Oy Nokia Ab.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358 9 680 50 245</p>
</text>
